    "narrative": "For May 31, 2026, the Austin Waves lineup is anchored by **Jackson Merrill**, whose 75.26 efficiency score against Littell represents our highest upside play. **Merrill** benefits from a favorable matchup against a starter with a 4.63 xERA, and despite the slight penalty for Littell's control over the running game, his position in the #5 spot provides ample RBI opportunity. Right behind him, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (73.66) and **Gunnar Henderson** (70.50) project as elite starts; **Garc\u00eda Jr.** capitalizes on a soft matchup against Canning, while **Henderson** leverages a high-park-factor environment to maintain high power output despite facing a challenging arm in Miles. **Kyle Tucker** (70.97) also remains a core staple, as his consistent plate discipline continues to stabilize the heart of our order.\n\nThe most difficult decision on today's card was the exclusion of **Liam Hicks** (39.57). While **Hicks** sits just below our \"marginal\" floor, he was the primary candidate to displace **Brayan Rocchio** (40.91). Ultimately, the optimizer prioritized **Rocchio** due to his defensive role and the remaining cushion in our game caps, whereas **Hicks** was penalized for a difficult matchup against McLean\u2019s 3.03 xERA and the volatility of his pending lineup status. Elsewhere, we are proceeding with caution regarding **Josh Jung**, **Andy Pages**, and **Kyle Tucker**; while these three are projected to start, their lineup positions are currently unconfirmed. Should their final order spots shift downward, their respective 58.59, 63.66, and 70.97 scores may experience minor downward adjustments, though all three retain enough situational value to remain in the starting nine regardless of minor batting order fluctuations.",
